From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] fb8: don't wait on a counter that may be stopped to blink the screen

The terminal emulator answers BEL with blink-screen, which on every fb8
display (cgthree, tcx, vga) is fb8-blink-screen: invert the screen,
"2000 ms", invert it back. ms polls get-msecs, which on sparc32 reads
the obp-ticks variable that only the firmware's own level-14 timer
interrupt handler (irq_entry14 in arch/sparc32/vectors.S) advances.

A client that writes its console through the firmware, as Solaris 2.x
and SunOS 4.1.4 do on a framebuffer console, has its own trap table by
then (and with this series' 0022 the romvec calls run at PIL 15 as
well). The firmware's handler never runs and obp-ticks stands still, so
the wait never ends: on the first BEL (bash's completion bell, echo of a
^G) the screen stays inverted and the console hangs. Solaris 2.6 on an
SS-5 with a cg3, after "echo ^G" in a single-user shell: TBR 0xf0040050
(the kernel's trap table), PSR PIL 15, the PC in the Forth inner
interpreter (semis, dovar, enterforth), and obp-ticks 20970 both times
it was read, 5 s apart.

Wait at most 100 ms on the counter, and leave the loop after 20000 reads
of it in any case (80 to 140 ms under TCG on the lab's host, where
100000 reads took 400 to 680 ms), so the blink ends whatever the client
has done to the trap table or the interrupt level. The 2000 was also a
hex number: the blink at the firmware's own prompt took 0x2000 = 8192
ms.

sun4u's obp-ticks stays 0 in this tree (get-msecs falls back to counting
its own calls), so the wait never hung there; the change keeps its blink
short as before.

While here, drop the flag execute-device-method leaves for the
"ring-bell" method that /screen doesn't have: every BEL left one cell on
the data stack ("0 > 7 emit ok" was followed by "1 >").
---
 forth/device/display.fs  | 12 +++++++++++-
 forth/device/terminal.fs |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/forth/device/display.fs b/forth/device/display.fs
index 010f9af..96432e3 100644
--- a/forth/device/display.fs
+++ b/forth/device/display.fs
@@ -257,8 +257,18 @@ defer fb8-invertrect
   fb8-invertrect
   ;
 
+\ The flash lasts up to 100 ms on the millisecond counter, and the wait
+\ also stops after a fixed number of reads of the counter: the counter is
+\ advanced by the firmware's own timer interrupt, which no longer runs once
+\ a client program has its own trap table (Solaris writes its console
+\ through the firmware), and a wait on the counter alone never ends there.
 : fb8-blink-screen ( -- )
-  fb8-invert-screen 2000 ms
+  fb8-invert-screen
+  get-msecs d# 100 +
+  d# 20000 0 do
+    dup get-msecs - 0< if leave then
+  loop
+  drop
   fb8-invert-screen
   ;
   
diff --git a/forth/device/terminal.fs b/forth/device/terminal.fs
index 24b2d10..435ddf7 100644
--- a/forth/device/terminal.fs
+++ b/forth/device/terminal.fs
@@ -236,7 +236,7 @@
   7 of \ BEL
     blink-screen
     s" /screen" s" ring-bell" 
-    execute-device-method
+    execute-device-method drop
   endof
   8 of \ BS
     column# 0<> if
